<title>UK: Bulker completes barley discharge at Saudi port.</title>
<headline>Bulker completes barley discharge at Saudi port.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulk carrier Qena, which went aground off Dammam at the end of January, completed discharging its cargo of grain at the Saudi Arabian port on Wednesday, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said.</p>
<p>The 38,319 dwt Egyptian flagged vessel was carrying 33,988 tonnes of barley.</p>
<p>Underwater inspection revealed only slight damage to the vessel and repairs were deferred.</p>
